  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1 class="page-hero__title">Texas Aerial Robotics</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Texas Aerial Robotics was founded in 2017 by a handful of UT
        students excited by the possibility of building a fully autonomous
        drone from scratch. That passion eventually led to TAR competing
        among top universities from around the world at the International
        Aerial Robotics Competition. Today, TAR provides undergraduate
        students with the opportunity and resources to work on cutting edge
        robotics.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===============================================================
       TECHNICAL SKILLS
       =============================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--light">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Technical skills</span>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <h2>Hands-on across the whole design process.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Our members do hands-on work with a variety of different skills
          across the design and development process.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="panel reveal">
          <p class="panel__title">
            <span class="icon icon--wrench" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            Hardware
          </p>
          <ul class="list-check">
            <li>CAD</li>
            <li>Drone Avionics</li>
            <li>Prototyping + Manufacturing</li>
            <li>PCB Design</li>
            <li>Embedded Electronics</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="panel reveal">
          <p class="panel__title">
            <span class="icon icon--code" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            Software
          </p>
          <ul class="list-check">
            <li>ROS (C++, Python)</li>
            <li>PX4</li>
            <li>Computer Vision</li>
            <li>Path Planning</li>
            <li>SLAM</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===============================================================
       THIS YEAR
       =============================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--dark section--grid">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">What we're working on this year</span>
          <hr class="rule" />
          <h2>From the ground up to full autonomy.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Our organization is dedicated to the design, development, and
            programming of a fully autonomous drone, with the goal of
            navigating a complex obstacle course by the end of the academic
            year. This ambitious project leverages the collaborative efforts
            of our hardware and software teams, working from the ground up
            to achieve full autonomy.
          </p>
          <p class="lede">
            In addition, we are proud to have a team participating in the
            prestigious RTX Autonomous Vehicles Competition. This
            competition presents a unique pursuit-evasion challenge, where
            both aerial and ground robots are employed in dynamic and
            strategic environments.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/projects.html"
              >Browse the projects</a
            >
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/ravg.html">RAVG team</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="panel reveal">
          <p class="panel__title">Sub-teams</p>
          <ul class="list-check">
            <li>
              <strong>Hardware</strong> &mdash; designs and manufactures the
              drone, mission-specific add-ons, and test rigs.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Computer Vision</strong> &mdash; everything to do with
              how the drone sees its surroundings.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Controls</strong> &mdash; the flight path management
              code that decides how the drone manoeuvres.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Simulations</strong> &mdash; catches bugs in vision
              and flight planning before anything leaves the ground.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Business</strong> &mdash; industry sponsorship, event
              planning, and social media.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===============================================================
       HISTORY
       =============================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--muted">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="eyebrow">History</span>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <h2>Where we've been.</h2>
      </div>

      <ol class="timeline">
        <li class="reveal">
          <p class="timeline__year">2017</p>
          <h3 class="timeline__title">Founded</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            A handful of UT students set out to build a fully autonomous
            drone from scratch.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <p class="timeline__year">IARC Mission 7</p>
          <h3 class="timeline__title">Herding ground robots</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Mission 7 took a monumental leap by requiring autonomous aerial
            robots to interact with and control autonomous ground robots,
            herding them out of an arena with no 3D cues such as walls.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <p class="timeline__year">IARC Mission 8</p>
          <h3 class="timeline__title">Swarms and QR fragments</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Teams had to control a swarm of drones that accepted commands
            through audio or visual input, piece together four fragments of
            a QR code, and avoid enemy drones &mdash; all without GPS.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <p class="timeline__year">IARC Mission 9</p>
          <h3 class="timeline__title">Repair at a distance</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Fly roughly two miles to a mast simulating a ship at sea,
            synchronise with it, swap a defective communications module, and
            return &mdash; in under nine minutes, using only onboard
            computing.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <p class="timeline__year">Today</p>
          <h3 class="timeline__title">Four project teams and RAVG</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Members build claw retrieval, thrust vectoring, and vision
            targeting systems while our competition team takes on the RTX
            Autonomous Vehicle Competition.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===============================================================
       OFFICERS
       The list itself lives in src/content/about-officer-team.txt.
       Edit that file to change who is on the team; nothing here needs
       touching, however many officers there are.
       =============================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--light">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="eyebrow">{{ site.season }} Officer Team</span>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <h2>Who runs TAR.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3">
        {%- for officer in officers %}
        <article class="card reveal">
          <p class="card__index">{{ officer.role }}</p>
          <h3 class="card__title">{{ officer.name }}</h3>
          {%- if officer.details.length or officer.email %}
          <p class="card__body">
            {{ officer.details | join(" · ") }}
            {%- if officer.details.length and officer.email %}<br />{% endif %}
            {%- if officer.email %}
            <a href="mailto:{{ officer.email }}">{{ officer.email }}</a>
            {%- endif %}
          </p>
          {%- endif %}
        </article>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2>Want to join?</h2>
      <p>
        We take new members every semester, from every major. Send us a
        message and we will tell you when the next info session is.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact.html">Contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
